<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Le Moyne d&apos;Iberville returns four weeks after starting treatment. He took all four doses of chloroquine, with mild nausea on the first day, and finished the 14 days of primaquine two weeks ago, taking it with food; he had mild stomach cramps for a few days and no dark urine, breathlessness or blue lips. He has had no fever. He did not have the smear and PCR that were meant for a week after the last primaquine dose, because the date was not booked. He explained the fever plan back correctly. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Chloroquine</td><td>All doses taken; mild nausea on the first day</td></tr><tr><td>Primaquine</td><td>14 days completed two weeks ago; mild stomach cramps</td></tr><tr><td>Fever</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Missed test</td><td>Post-treatment smear and PCR not done</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

